# Keep shell scripts LF-only, even in a Windows working tree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: Git on Windows usually runs with core.autocrlf=true,
# which rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for YAML and Markdown,
# but it breaks any script that runs inside a Linux container: the shebang
# becomes "#!/bin/sh\r", Linux looks for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/sh\r", and Docker reports the missing *interpreter* as
#
#     exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# ...which reads like the script is absent when it is sitting right there.
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for these paths so the copy on disk — the copy you
# upload to your practice repo — is already LF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
